{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.IdempotentTraceRigidity","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basis","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Lemmas"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.conj_of_isPreconnected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.conj_of_isPreconnected","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L282-L302","doc":"**Rigidity comparison.** Let `x ↦ φ_x, ψ_x : ∏ Matrix →ₐ[ℂ] Matrix n n ℂ` be two families\nwhose base idempotents `φ_x(u i o o)`, `ψ_x(u i o o)` are continuous on a preconnected set `S`.\nIf `φ_{x₀}` and `ψ_{x₀}` are conjugate for one `x₀ ∈ S`, then `φ_x` and `ψ_x` are conjugate for\nevery `x ∈ S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.isIdempotentElem_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.isIdempotentElem_unit","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L279-L280","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.rank_eq_of_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.rank_eq_of_conj","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L257-L267","doc":"Conjugate representations have equal block ranks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.exists_conj_of_rank_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.exists_conj_of_rank_eq","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L230-L255","doc":"**Matrix form.** Two algebra maps `∏ Matrix →ₐ Matrix n n K` whose base idempotents have the\nsame ranks are conjugate by an invertible matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.mult_toLin_finrank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.mult_toLin_finrank","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L225-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.exists_intertwiner_of_finrank_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.exists_intertwiner_of_finrank_eq","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L197-L213","doc":"**Two representations of `∏ Matrix` with equal multiplicities are isomorphic.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.decomp_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.decomp_map","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoComparison.lean#L185-L191","doc":"**The decomposition intertwines `φ` with the standard action.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.decomp_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KohnoComparison.decomp_apply","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KohnoCom